  words:
  - lepidoptera
  - lepidopteras
  info: 'Lepidoptera is an order of winged insects that includes butterflies and
    moths. Approximately 180,000 species of Lepidoptera have been described, accounting
    for about 10% of all described species. Butterflies and moths lay eggs on plants,
    which hatch into larvae called caterpillars. As they mature, caterpillars form
    a pupa; some spin a silk casing called a cocoon, while others form a chrysalis
    or develop underground. During this stage, they undergo metamorphosis and transition
    into their adult butterfly or moth form.


    Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lepidoptera '
  image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: ff3b07490e6358246b34bf54313c079e, type: 3}
